WEBVTT

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.230
Again?

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:17.320
You're pathetic.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.400
Think he's doing it deliberately?

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:24.900
If there was a girl watching,
I'd be taking this more seriously.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.440
Don't make excuses.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.230
I mean it!

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:30.900
What's important is your concentration, right?

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:35.940
If you can only do your best
when a girl's watching...

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:38.820
You're helpless anyway.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.280
Panty flash!

00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:48.070
What do you want to eat?

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:49.360
Some sit-down restaurant chain?

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:50.780
No.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:52.650
I mean which chain.

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:57.820
"Exhibition of Unforgettable Literature"

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:54.440
I vote ramen.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:56.900
Ramen doesn't count.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:03.400
Yoji!

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:06.110
What are you doing?

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:07.530
Sorry, sorry.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:10.960
"Exhibition of Unforgettable Literature"

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:46.480
"Setting Sun"

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:49.690
Settling... Sun?

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:51.530
You missed your stop?

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:53.320
And that's why you're late?

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:55.070
Were you too focused on your video game?

00:03:55.070 --> 00:03:56.320
No.

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:58.820
Then was there a pretty girl?

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:00.150
No!

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:02.260
"Library"

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.980
Settling... Settling...

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:09.900
There're too many books!
I have no idea where it could be.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:11.310
"Ango Sakaguchi" "Sakunosuke Oda"

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:13.820
"Sakutaro Hagiwara"

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.820
Wait, it's organized by author?

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:17.900
<i>Settling Sun</i> ... Who wrote it?

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.820
<i>Setting Sun</i> .

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:24.190
The name of the book is <i>Setting Sun</i> .

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:27.150
How could you get that wrong?

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:28.150
Who are you?

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:30.570
The author is Osamu Dazai.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:33.610
You don't know him?
He's incredibly famous!

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:34.900
Dazai?

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:36.780
Remember the name.

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:37.860
Dazai.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:39.900
Da. Za. I.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:42.150
It's over there.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:50.230
He was weird, and weirdly dressed.

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:54.110
"Setting Sun"

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:01.610
Wake up!

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:04.690
I can't believe it!

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:07.940
You fell asleep reading one of my books?
Impossible!

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:11.440
How did you get in here?

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:13.230
Finish the damn book.

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:16.780
Someone with a brain like yours
is going to forget it all immediately.

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:19.570
So you need to read the whole thing
at once or you'll just forget.

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:24.070
Wh-Who are you?

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:29.150
If you don't finish the book,
you won't be able to talk to them, right?

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:30.780
Shut up.

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:32.820
And anyway, you...

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:33.820
Huh?

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:39.810
"Setting Sun"

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:01.280
That book...

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:04.070
It's great, huh?

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:10.190
We've got similar tastes.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:27.280
"Exhibition of Unforgettable Literature"

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:34.320
Osamu Dazai was born to be an author.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:30.030
"Chuya Nakahara"

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:38.230
He caused no end of trouble
for friends by going into debt.

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:40.940
When he couldn't pay his bar tab or inn tab,

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:46.110
he left Kazuo Dan at the inn
and went to Tokyo to get money,

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:48.360
but Dazai never came back.

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:49.940
Why?

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:53.280
When Kazuo Dan got annoyed
and went to Tokyo to look for him,

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:57.730
he found him playing shogi with Masuji Ibuse.

00:06:57.730 --> 00:07:01.780
Like he'd forgotten he'd
ever left his friend behind.

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:03.530
What a dick!

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:04.570
Shut up!

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:06.190
I didn't forget!

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:15.080
"Osamu Dazai"

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:11.110
There's no end of episodes

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:15.320
from Osamu Dazai's life
that show what a degenerate he is.

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:18.230
He failed at two lovers' suicides,

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:21.780
killing both women.

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:23.900
What a loser.

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:25.320
Yeah.

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:30.440
There's no denying he's a loser
who couldn't get along with others.

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:32.280
But...

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:34.400
...his works are wonderful.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:37.570
Did he write all these?

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:40.730
If you ask me, it's simple.

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:45.650
Osamu Dazai just lacked the ability
to get along in society.

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:47.320
But even so...

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:49.320
No, because of that,

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:53.230
he was able to leave all these
wonderful works for the world.

00:07:53.230 --> 00:07:56.570
He could write books because he was a loser?

00:07:56.570 --> 00:08:03.650
Someone who's a slave to society
could never write a work that shocked it.

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:07.230
That's what I think, anyway.

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:10.360
Wait!

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:15.070
When night falls, the moon feels so close here.

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:19.320
Even without the streetlights,
you can read books by the moonlight.

00:08:19.320 --> 00:08:22.650
You really like books.

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:24.070
Is that weird?

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:25.230
No.

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:27.690
It's like...

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:29.440
I'm jealous.

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:31.280
Of books.

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:32.400
Of books?

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:36.570
You only care about books.

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:45.570
I'll leave you behind!

00:08:46.570 --> 00:08:53.820
I was happy... when you said you
liked <i>Setting Sun</i> . The book.

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:57.980
This world is overflowing with entertainment.

00:08:57.980 --> 00:09:01.730
Just looking at your phone
will connect you to the world.

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:05.530
You have access to the finest
works the world's ever produced.

00:09:05.530 --> 00:09:11.530
In the modern world, it's so rare
for people to choose books...

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:14.940
I'm not like that.

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:16.440
It was just chance.

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:21.280
No matter what the reason is,
it's wonderful that you like books.

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:26.360
And if possible, I want you to read more.

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:27.860
More?

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:32.440
Every type of creative work is a light
that makes your life wonderful.

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:35.900
For me, that light was books.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:38.650
I'd be happy if that was true for you.

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:46.320
Today, let's learn about
the writing of Chuya Nakahara.

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:50.400
Nakahara? He was in that exhibition.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:53.610
I'm a big fan of his.

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:56.980
And if you asked me what makes him special,

00:09:56.980 --> 00:10:00.900
I would say it's his skill at picking words.

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:03.820
He uses a limited amount of words to describe

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:06.480
an incredible amount of meaning.

00:10:06.480 --> 00:10:10.650
Nobody has his level of talent
when it comes to this...

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:12.900
That guy gets it.

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:20.070
What's wrong?

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:22.230
No, nothing.

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:25.530
You idiot! You got this part wrong!

00:10:25.530 --> 00:10:29.320
How dumb do you have to be to screw up my poem?

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:31.610
Fix it!

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:34.690
Read books besides those of Osamu Dazai.

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:37.900
I wonder which one fits you best.

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:42.690
That's my book! You've got good taste!

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:47.360
Boy, a man's life is defined by his failure.

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:51.440
If you want to learn more,
I suggest you read my books.

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:56.570
Listen, Ango, not everyone
wants to live like you do.

00:10:56.570 --> 00:10:57.980
What?

00:10:57.980 --> 00:10:59.980
Corruption is the one constant of life.

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:01.940
In every era and every place,

00:11:01.940 --> 00:11:04.030
man is condemned to corruption.

00:11:04.030 --> 00:11:08.780
I say he should know that there's more to life!

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:13.360
If you have a path to follow,
you don't need other possibilities.

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:15.360
You want a fight?

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:16.650
Do you?

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:19.950
"Setting Sun"

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:25.980
Listen, I still think I should've
won the Akutagawa Prize.

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:27.150
Why?

00:11:27.150 --> 00:11:30.190
Because I respect him the most!

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:32.280
What's that got to do with the prize?

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:34.690
A lot!

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:38.360
But I don't know if that justifies
writing a four-meter long

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:40.730
letter to Haruo Sato!

00:11:40.730 --> 00:11:41.980
How'd you know about that?

00:11:41.980 --> 00:11:43.030
It's a famous story!

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:44.400
It is?

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:49.940
My delicate and stylish image!

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:57.530
Did I imagine it?

00:11:57.980 --> 00:12:00.940
"Setting Sun"

00:12:57.110 --> 00:13:01.940
The only reason I didn't break down
crying here was books, maybe.

00:13:02.980 --> 00:13:06.440
I'm a failure too, you see.

00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:09.110
At living in this world.

00:13:09.110 --> 00:13:14.440
With all its entertainment,
this world has no end of fun things.

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:17.780
Many people share that fun with others.

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:22.440
They connect with them and find
satisfaction within that happiness.

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:27.650
But for some reason, I can't be a part of that.

00:13:27.650 --> 00:13:32.940
I can't find fun or value in that.

00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:37.030
I don't have the right to deny
the majority their fun.

00:13:37.030 --> 00:13:40.570
I'm sure it's the ones like them,

00:13:40.570 --> 00:13:43.440
who share their entertainment
and connect with one another,

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:45.820
who are living their lives
properly in this world.

00:13:45.820 --> 00:13:48.900
I'm the one who's wrong.

00:13:48.900 --> 00:13:51.030
That's not true.

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:57.280
And it was when I was upset
about this that I met Osamu Dazai.

00:13:57.280 --> 00:13:59.940
The first book I read was <i>No Longer Human</i> .

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:04.440
When I finished...
no, even when I was reading it...

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:07.150
My heart was enraptured.

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:09.650
It was strange.

00:14:09.650 --> 00:14:12.820
I'm nothing like the protagonist of that story.

00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:14.280
I can't sympathize with him.

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:20.400
But the way he had no choice but
to live his life as a fool and then die...

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:22.730
It felt so noble to me.

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:24.030
Noble?

00:14:24.030 --> 00:14:25.110
Yes.

00:14:25.110 --> 00:14:27.360
He may have been a failure as a human,

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:31.110
but the way he lived his life
was attractive to me, and noble.

00:14:31.110 --> 00:14:34.030
At least, that's how it felt to me.

00:14:34.030 --> 00:14:35.940
Which means...

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:37.900
Perhaps,

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:41.400
I could change my failure of a life
into something that I found attractive.

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:46.570
Even if to the rest of the world,
I wasn't even human.

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:52.820
Meeting that one book changed how I thought.

00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:54.190
That's amazing.

00:14:54.190 --> 00:14:58.440
Yeah. Osamu Dazai is really wonderful.

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:03.530
I thought my life was worthless,
and he gave it value.

00:15:03.530 --> 00:15:07.780
No, it's you who's amazing, Haruka.

00:15:07.780 --> 00:15:08.780
Me?

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:11.820
If you got all that from a single book,

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:15.150
it must mean you have an amazing heart.

00:15:15.150 --> 00:15:16.980
Yoji?

00:15:16.980 --> 00:15:18.610
Value, huh?

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:22.860
Maybe I found value in books, too.

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:24.610
Because they brought me to you.

00:15:38.820 --> 00:15:40.690
Hey.

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:41.730
Thanks.

00:15:43.190 --> 00:15:44.440
For what?

00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:46.150
Nothing.

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:51.680
"No Longer Human"

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:03.690
Today we'll be learning...

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:06.280
What, again?

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:08.230
"The Circus"

00:16:20.190 --> 00:16:21.940
Haruka! Haruka!

00:16:22.780 --> 00:16:23.820
Yoji?

00:16:23.820 --> 00:16:25.480
Something's wrong.

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:29.940
What should be here isn't...
But I don't know what it is!

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:31.110
Yoji...

00:16:31.110 --> 00:16:33.190
But I know it was here!

00:16:33.190 --> 00:16:35.650
Something that taught me something important!

00:16:35.650 --> 00:16:38.900
Something that created something inside me.

00:16:38.900 --> 00:16:41.320
Yoji... I'm sorry.

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:45.110
Haruka?

00:16:45.110 --> 00:16:49.190
I don't want to talk now.

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:50.190
Haruka!

00:16:59.730 --> 00:17:00.730
Why?

00:17:02.780 --> 00:17:03.780
How?

00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:12.820
Haruka...

00:17:12.820 --> 00:17:18.280
The phone number you have dialed
is unavailable or not in service...

00:17:19.690 --> 00:17:21.690
Haruka...

00:17:21.690 --> 00:17:26.400
Something inside me disappeared.

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:31.150
It disappeared from within
everyone else as well.

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:33.320
Why?

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:35.900
My heart feels so dry.

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:37.320
Why?

00:17:45.320 --> 00:17:46.650
Haruka!

00:17:47.360 --> 00:17:48.730
Haruka!

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:07.230
I'm a failure...

00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:10.820
...at living in this world.

00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:09.320
"Dumbass"

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:20.150
But even so... something gave me hope.

00:18:20.150 --> 00:18:23.690
Made me think my life had value.

00:18:23.690 --> 00:18:27.780
But it's gone.

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:30.940
It's nowhere to be found.

00:18:39.030 --> 00:18:40.690
I'm no longer...

00:18:55.400 --> 00:18:56.440
Haruka?

00:19:30.610 --> 00:19:32.940
What is literature?

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:37.980
It's not something you need to live.

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:40.820
But this is what I think.

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:46.730
The world's literature is making
someone's heart a wonderful place.

00:19:46.730 --> 00:19:49.280
Literature isn't necessary.

00:19:49.280 --> 00:19:55.690
But a world without literature
must be a very boring place.

00:19:50.030 --> 00:19:53.030
"Portrait of Hell"

00:19:53.030 --> 00:19:53.920
"Japanese Literature"

00:19:56.650 --> 00:20:00.780
That sense of stifling confinement, I think,

00:20:00.780 --> 00:20:03.980
will slowly destroy the world...

00:20:10.940 --> 00:20:11.980
A dream?

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:16.400
You finally woke up?

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:20.360
I'd love to go back to bed if I got the chance.

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:24.030
I'm afraid there's no time.

00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:26.900
Look around you.

00:20:26.900 --> 00:20:28.570
Unbelievable.

00:20:28.570 --> 00:20:31.530
I'm never the first to awake.

00:20:31.530 --> 00:20:32.860
So I'm in a book?

00:20:32.860 --> 00:20:33.820
Yes.

00:20:33.820 --> 00:20:39.070
After delving, you were almost
immediately defeated by a Taint...

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:42.610
...and devoured by the world.

00:20:42.610 --> 00:20:47.480
I had to go inside your minds to awaken you.

00:20:47.480 --> 00:20:49.940
The method I chose was a dream.

00:20:49.940 --> 00:20:52.650
It wasn't clear if it would work.

00:20:52.650 --> 00:20:54.440
Why was I the only one to dream?

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:55.730
I don't know.

00:20:55.730 --> 00:21:02.480
Perhaps you're more closely connected
to the Alchemist than the others.

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:05.780
So the Alchemist created that dream?

00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:06.820
Yes.

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:09.820
A world where books were tainted and destroyed.

00:21:09.820 --> 00:21:15.190
Whether that despair was imaginary or not,
for the Alchemist...

00:21:15.190 --> 00:21:19.400
Gods of Agni, will you lend me your aid?

00:21:19.400 --> 00:21:21.400
No more explanation.

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:25.820
Tell the Alchemist I want
a better dream next time.

00:21:25.820 --> 00:21:28.400
It was quite unpleasant.

00:21:28.400 --> 00:21:33.940
But that's why it must be saved.

00:21:33.940 --> 00:21:35.150
Indeed.

00:21:35.150 --> 00:21:39.570
I entrust the fate of this book to you.

00:21:36.820 --> 00:21:39.570
"Howl at the Moon"

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:44.650
Huh? Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> ?

00:21:44.650 --> 00:21:45.940
Where are we?

00:21:50.610 --> 00:21:53.280
What is this place?

00:21:50.610 --> 00:21:53.280
Hey! What are you doing?

00:21:53.280 --> 00:21:55.860
Oww! Oww! Don't pull me!

00:21:55.860 --> 00:21:56.900
Stop it!

00:21:56.900 --> 00:21:59.920
"Howl at the Moon"

00:23:30.570 --> 00:23:32.070
Literary Gourmet!

00:23:32.070 --> 00:23:34.940
The Ultra-High-Calorie Beef and Rice Chapter!

00:23:34.940 --> 00:23:37.150
If only I had more muscles...

00:23:37.150 --> 00:23:39.980
You there, who wants more muscles.

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:41.650
What do you want, peach flower boy?

00:23:41.650 --> 00:23:44.650
I've got the perfect meal for you!

00:23:44.650 --> 00:23:46.530
Beef and Rice!

00:23:45.360 --> 00:23:49.530
"Beef and Rice"
"A rice bowl loaded with delicious beef.
Got its start when somebody put beef on rice."

00:23:46.530 --> 00:23:49.150
Yeah, it looks like an easy source of protein!

00:23:49.150 --> 00:23:51.440
We start by adding butter.

00:23:51.440 --> 00:23:52.900
Then fried pork and curry.

00:23:52.900 --> 00:23:54.070
French fries.

00:23:54.070 --> 00:23:54.940
Chicken wings.

00:23:54.940 --> 00:23:56.780
Then top with mayo!

00:23:56.780 --> 00:23:57.900
And it's done!

00:23:57.900 --> 00:23:59.440
I can't eat that!
